								<string name="Name">IMPORTANT</string>
								<string name="Source">--IMPORTANT!

--For these to work with the script I made, you must make sure the name of the counters are
--&quot;Coals: 0&quot; and &quot;Diamonds: 0&quot;. This makes the script find them at the start of the game so they
--can be used for counting!</string>
								<bool name="archivable">true</bool>
							</Properties>
						</Item>
					</Item>
					<Item class="Script" referent="RBX1397">
						<Properties>
							<bool name="Disabled">false</bool>
							<Content name="LinkedSource"><null></null></Content>
							<string name="Name">README</string>
							<string name="Source">--OWNER-ONLY version. Only the owner of the factory can use it! For purposes of demonstration,
--I have made it so that anyone who touches the owner button becomes the new owner.
--REMEMBER TO READ THE README FOR THE COUNTERS TOO! ITS IN THE COUNTERS-MODEL!

--For this to work you must do these things!

--Make a small black brick, and name it &quot;PieceOfCoal&quot; exactly as it says. NOT &quot;pieceofcoal&quot; or &quot;PIECEOFCOAL&quot;.
--Place this brick where you want it to spawn (under the spawning machine).
--Make the brick part of the model &quot;TinyFactoryDemo&quot;
--If there is already a coal in this model, then you don&apos;t need to do these steps to make it work.


--ABOUT THE COUNTERS
--Read the README in the COUNTERS-model

--Also remember, making an &quot;advanced&quot; factory like the Bread factory tycoon factories is NOT easy for
--anyone that is not very experienced in scripting for roblox. Don&apos;t start it unless you have a good idea
--about what scripting is all about, and feel good about your scripting skills. 

--Uberubert</string>
							<bool name="archivable">true</bool>
						</Properties>
